{
  "title": "75: al-Qeyaamah القيامة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِيَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِۙ‏(1)\nLAA UQSEMO BE-YAWMID QEYAAMATE.\nNay! I swear by the Day of Resurrection!\nوَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِالنَّفْسِ اللَّوَّامَةِؕ‏(2)\nWA LAA UQSEMO BEALNNAFSE AL-LAWAMATE.\nNay! I swear by the Self- Accusing self!\nاَيَحْسَبُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَلَّنْ نَّجْمَعَ عِظَامَهٗؕ‏(3)\nA-YAHSABO INSAANO AALLAN NNAJMAA’A E’EZAAMAH.\nWhat! thinketh man that never will We assemble his bones?\nبَلٰى قٰدِرِيْنَ عَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّسَوِّىَ بَنَانَهٗ‏(4)\nBALAA QAADEREENA A’LAA AN NNUSAWAAA BANAANAH.\nYea! We can put in complete order even his very finger tips (with the prints thereon)!\nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ الْاِنْسَانُ لِيَفْجُرَ اَمَامَهٗ‌ۚ‏(5)\nBAL YOREEDO INSAANO LEEFJURA AAMAAMAH.\nNay! but willeth man (always) to do evil (even) before him\nيَسْئَلُ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ‏(6)\nYASALU AYYAANA YAWMUD AL-QEEMATE.\nAsketh he: “When is the Day of Resurrection (to come)?\nفَاِذَا بَرِقَ الْبَصَرُۙ‏(7)\nFA-EZAA BAREQA BASARO.\nSo when confounded shall be the eye\nوَخَسَفَ الْقَمَرُۙ‏(8)\nWAKHASAFA AL-QAMARU.\nAnd when darkened shall be the moon\nوَجُمِعَ الشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُۙ‏(9)\nWAJUMEA’A YANBAGHEE WAL-QAMARO.\nAnd shall be brought together the sun and the moon\nيَقُوْلُ الْاِنْسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ اَيْنَ الْمَفَرُّ‌ ۚ‏(10)\nYAQOOLO INSAANO YAWMA-EZIN AYNA AL-MAFARRU.\nMan shall cry that day: “Where is place to flee to?\nكَلَّا لَا وَزَرَؕ‏(11)\nKALLAA LAA WAZARA.\nBy no means! No place shall there be of any refuge!\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْمُسْتَقَرُّ ؕ‏(12)\nELAA RABBEKA YAWMAEZE AL-MUSTAQARRU.\nUnto thy Lord (alone) shall be the place of rest!\nيُنَبَّؤُا الْاِنْسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَ وَاَخَّرَؕ‏(13)\nYUNABBAUA INSAANO YAWMA-EZIN BEMAA QADDAMA WAAKKHARA.\nMan shall be informed on that day of whatsoever he put before and whatsoever he put behind!\nبَلِ الْاِنْسَانُ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖ بَصِيْرَةٌ ۙ‏(14)\nBALIL INSAANO A’LAA WA BASEERATUN.\nNay! (there is no need as) man against his own self shall be a witness!\nوَّلَوْ اَلْقٰى مَعَاذِيْرَهٗؕ‏(15)\nWA LAW AALQAA MAA’AAZEERAH.\nAnd even if he put forth his excuses!\nلَا تُحَرِّكْ بِهٖ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهٖؕ‏(16)\nLAA TUHARREK BEHI LESAANAKA LETAA’JALA BEH.\n(O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Move not thy tongue with it (the Qur’an) in haste!\nاِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهٗ وَقُرْاٰنَهٗۚ  ۖ‏(17)\nINNAL A’LAYNAA JAMA’AH WAQURAAANAH.\nVerily, on Us is the collection of it and the recital of it!\nفَاِذَا قَرَاْنٰهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْاٰنَهٗ‌ۚ‏(18)\nFA-EZAA QARAANAAHU FAATTABEA’ QURAAANAH.\nSo, when We have recited it, then follow thou the recital!\nثُمَّ اِنَّ عَلَيْنَا بَيَانَهٗؕ‏(19)\nSUMMA INNAL A’LAYNAA BAYAANAH.\nAgain, it is on Us the explaining of it!\nكَلَّا بَلْ تُحِبُّوْنَ الْعَاجِلَةَ ۙ‏(20)\nKALLAA BAL TUHEBBOONA A’AJELATA.\nNay! But ye love the fleeing life!\nوَتَذَرُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(21)\nWATAZAROONA AAKHERATA.\nAnd neglect ye the hereafter!\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ نَّاضِرَةٌ ۙ‏(22)\nWOJOOHUN-Y YAWMA-EZIN NNAAZERATUN.\n(Some?) faces on that day shall be resplendent!\nاِلٰى رَبِّهَا نَاظِرَةٌ‌ ۚ‏(23)\nELAA RABBEHAA NAAZERATUN.\nUnto their Lord (they will be) attentive!\nوَوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍۢ بَاسِرَةٌ ۙ‏(24)\nWA WOJOOHINY YAWMA-EZIN BAASERATUN.\nAnd (other) faces on that day shall be despondent\nتَظُنُّ اَنْ يُّفْعَلَ بِهَا فَاقِرَةٌ ؕ‏(25)\nTAZUNNU AN YYUFA’ALA BEHAA FAAQERATUN.\nThinking that would befall them some great calamity\nكَلَّاۤ اِذَا بَلَغَتِ التَّرَاقِىَۙ‏(26)\nKALLAA EZAA BALAGHATIL AT-TARAAQEAAA.\nNay! When it (life) shall reach the throat\nوَقِيْلَ مَنْ رَاقٍۙ‏(27)\nWA QEELAD MAN RAAQIN.\nAnd it will be said: “Who is the charmer ”?\nوَّظَنَّ اَنَّهُ الْفِرَاقُۙ‏(28)\nWWAZANNA ANNAHUL AL-FERAAQU.\nAnd realiseth man that it is the (hour of) parting!\nوَالْتَفَّتِ السَّاقُ بِالسَّاقِۙ‏(29)\nWAL TAFFATE AS-SAAQU BEALSSAAQE.\nAnd when one leg (will twist) with the other leg, (When the agony is heaped on agony)\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْمَسَاقُؕ‏(30)\nELAA RABBEKA YAWMAEZE AL-MASAAQU.\nUnto thy Lord on that day shall be the drive!\nفَلَا صَدَّقَ وَلَا صَلّٰىۙ‏(31)\nFALAA SADDAQA WA LAA SALLAA.\nFor he believed not in the Truth, nor did he offer the regular prayers\nوَلٰڪِنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىۙ‏(32)\nWALAAN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nBut belied the Truth and turned he away\nثُمَّ ذَهَبَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ يَتَمَطّٰىؕ‏(33)\nSUMMA ZAHABAL ELAA AHLEHI YATAMATTAA.\nThen went he unto his people in haughtiness\nاَوْلٰى لَكَ فَاَوْلٰىۙ‏(34)\nAAWLAA LAKA FAAWLAA.\nNearer unto thee (O’ man!) is destruction and nearer still!\nثُمَّ اَوْلٰى لَكَ فَاَوْلٰىؕ‏(35)\nSUMMA AAWLAA LAKA FAAWLAA.\nAgain, nearer unto thee (O’ man!) the destruction and nearer still!\nاَيَحْسَبُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنْ يُّتْرَكَ سُدًىؕ‏(36)\nA-YAHSABO INSAANO AN YYUTRAKA SUDAN.\nWhat! Thinkest man that he will be left uncontrolled?\nاَلَمْ يَكُ نُطْفَةً مِّنْ مَّنِىٍّ يُّمْنٰىۙ‏(37)\nALAM YAKU NUTFATAN MIN MMANEAAAIN YYUMNAA.\nWas he not a (mere) drop of sperm emitted?\nثُمَّ كَانَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقَ فَسَوّٰىۙ‏(38)\nSUMMA KAANA A’ALAQATAN FA KHALAQAL FASAWWAA.\nThen was he a clot of blood, then He created (him), and (He) made (him) proportioned\nفَجَعَلَ مِنْهُ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىؕ‏(39)\nFA-JA-A’LA MINHO AZ-ZAWJAYNE KHALAQAZ WAL AUNSAA.\nThen made He of him of two kinds, the male and the female\nاَلَيْسَ ذٰلِكَ بِقٰدِرٍ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يُّحْىِۦَ الْمَوْتٰى‏(40)\nA-LAYSA ZAALEKA WAL-ARZA A’LAA AN YYUHAAA MAWTAA.\nWhat! Is not He potent enough to give life (again) unto the dead?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qeyaamah (The Resurrection)\nThis Surah has 40 verses and it is ‘Makki’. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites this Surah will be counted from among those who believed in the Day of Judgement and his face will be shining when he is raised from his grave. It is also narrated that frequent reciters will be raised with handsome and attractive faces on the Day of Judgement.\nRecitation of this Surah increases sustenance and protects the life and possessions of the reciter. He is liked by people. Surah al-Qeyaamah also makes a person chaste, humble and sincere. Drinking water in which this Surah has been written keeps the heart safe from ailments."
